# Local machine configuration for TRELLIS-AMD (gfx1151 / Strix Halo).
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then edit
#
# `.env` is gitignored — put machine-specific paths here, never in tracked files.
# Everything below is OPTIONAL: env_amd.sh auto-detects sane values and only uses
# these as overrides. Format is plain KEY=VALUE; `#` starts a comment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weight caches
#
# No model weights live in this repo — roughly 10.5 GB is fetched on first use and
# cached. There are THREE independent caches:
#
#   TRELLIS_HF_HOME     -> HF_HOME     TRELLIS checkpoints + CLIP text encoder
#                                      (image ~3.1 GB, text ~3.9 GB + 642 MB,
#                                       CLIP ~1.6 GB)
#   TRELLIS_TORCH_HOME  -> TORCH_HOME  DINOv2 image encoder, via torch.hub (~1.2 GB)
#   TRELLIS_U2NET_HOME  -> U2NET_HOME  rembg's u2net.onnx background remover (~168 MB)
#
# Setting only HF_HOME is a common mistake — it covers NEITHER of the other two, so
# DINOv2 (1.2 GB) quietly lands in ~/.cache/torch and u2net (168 MB) in ~/.u2net.
#
# Leave blank to use each library's default
# (~/.cache/huggingface, ~/.cache/torch, ~/.u2net).
#TRELLIS_HF_HOME=/path/to/models/hf-cache
#TRELLIS_TORCH_HOME=/path/to/models/torch-cache
#TRELLIS_U2NET_HOME=/path/to/models/u2net-cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# System HSA runtime to LD_PRELOAD (the critical gfx1151 fix)
#
# The ROCm HSA runtime bundled in the PyTorch wheel segfaults on gfx1151 during
# HSA queue creation; the system one does not. env_amd.sh searches
# $ROCM_PATH/lib and /opt/rocm{,/core-*}/lib automatically — only set this if
# your ROCm is installed somewhere unusual.
#
# Find it with:  find /opt/rocm -name 'libhsa-runtime64.so.1'
#TRELLIS_HSA_RUNTIME=/opt/rocm/lib/libhsa-runtime64.so.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROCm / GPU overrides (normally auto-detected)
#
# ROCM_HOME is resolved from /opt/rocm/include, which is a symlink into a
# versioned component dir. PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH comes from `rocminfo`.
#ROCM_HOME=/opt/rocm
#PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH=gfx1151

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradio server (defaults to loopback only — no public tunnel)
#
# Upstream shipped 0.0.0.0 + share=True, which exposes your GPU publicly.
# Change these only if you deliberately want that.
#GRADIO_SERVER_NAME=127.0.0.1
#GRADIO_SERVER_PORT=7860
#GRADIO_SHARE=0
